  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Remnant Bei tribe higher-ups hide near the field after their camp falls. Their leader Bei Cao Chuan sighs that Zheng tribe is finished, reads Fang Yuan’s pressure under the Chang Shan Yin name as wise, and refuses a rush to retake the empty camp or burn Ge tribe rations while captives still live. He holds rank four among rank three elders, and the same stretch places him at about thirty with deep prestige inside the tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        481
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_bei_tribe",
        "fac_zheng_tribe",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_chang_shan_yin",
        "fac_ge_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is about thirty.",
      "chapters": [
        481
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He wears armor.",
      "chapters": [
        533
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "As a youth he was the least likely heir, kept a low profile while siblings fought, and waited until the old Bei tribe leader needed a healing Gu from a spirit rhino myriad beast king. He buried himself in a mud swamp for seven days, endured a crushed leg without a sound, stole the wild Gu, and hopped back on one leg to save his father. That act revealed rank three peak stage cultivation, won him the young tribe leader seat, and later the tribe leader seat as he expanded Bei tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        481
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rise-inside-bei-tribe",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_healing_gu",
        "sys_wild_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He brings Bei tribe elders to Wang tribe when Ge tribe’s strike has already made him a vagabond leader, and Pei Yan Fei’s side is named among the same crescent-lake fallout.",
      "chapters": [
        484
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-the-camp-loss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_wang_tribe",
        "char_pei_yan_fei"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the later field against Ge tribe he directs Bei and Zheng elders, waits for a chance to kill Chang Shan Yin rather than waste the one strike, and watches Pei Yan Fei’s Golden Rainbow Strike while revising his own plan as the wolf group shifts.",
      "chapters": [
        483
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-the-camp-loss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_golden_rainbow_strike"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later classes Liu tribe’s strongest enslavement expert as Bei Cao Chuan and treats his grass soldier troops as unimportant beside higher ranked Gu Masters.",
      "chapters": [
        527
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-the-camp-loss",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_liu_tribe",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the Liu tribe fight against Hei Lou Lan, Bei tribe elder Bei Cao Sheng entrusts his soul to Bei Cao Chuan. Using Liu Wen Wu’s Gu worm, Bei Cao Chuan absorbs that soul power and briefly reaches enslavement path master attainment, though he can last only seven minutes and expects impure soul damage afterward. The text names him originally a rank four enslavement path Gu Master and Bei tribe leader. He grows grass into rank two grass soldier puppets, advances some through rattan shell grass soldiers into rank four grass sword elite soldiers, and holds Fang Yuan’s mutated wolf group for a short stretch.",
      "chapters": [
        532
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grass-soldiers-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_hei_lou_lan",
        "char_bei_cao_sheng",
        "gu_liu_wen_wus_gu_worm",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan amplifies a wolf howl, the grass army shreds in a few breaths. A frenzy wolf tears Bei Cao Chuan’s throat, and three white-eyes wolves leave him a corpse torn into pieces.",
      "chapters": [
        533
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grass-soldiers-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes Bei Cao Chuan. No Chinese characters for the personal name appear in the English chapter text used here.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
